mutant: m065_follower_hides_newest_hot_batch
target: internal/catalog/follower/tick.go
failure-mode: |
  The follower builds Main's tail view without its newest hot batch. The
  batch is committed and acknowledged, but no pod serves it until a later
  commit or fold covers it, and the archive's last events stay invisible
  once traffic stops.
expected-detection: |
  Predicted: the layer 3 oracle waits for every pod's live observers to
  reach the catalog tip, and the hidden tail batch never reaches them.
  First run: the oracle missed it. Once traffic stops, BlockMaxAge (30s)
  folds the open block, which reveals the batch within the 2-minute
  convergence wait. The oracle now requires pods to serve a quiescent,
  complete catalog within disaggServeTimeout (10s), and kills it on every
  seed. TestFollower_LogMatchesCommittedStream pins the follower alone.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

